# JavaScript Code to Remove "(age X)" Pattern

Here are several ways to remove the "(age X)" pattern where X can be any number:

## Method 1: Using Regular Expression with `replace()`

```javascript
const text = "july 7 1994 (age 7) London, UK (1994-07-07)";

// Remove (age X) where X is any number
const result = text.replace(/\(age \d+\)/g, '').trim();

console.log(result);
// Output: "july 7 1994  London, UK (1994-07-07)"
```

## Method 2: Cleaner Output (remove extra spaces)

```javascript
const text = "july 7 1994 (age 7) London, UK (1994-07-07)";

// Remove (age X) and clean up extra spaces
const result = text.replace(/\s*\(age \d+\)\s*/g, ' ').trim();

console.log(result);
// Output: "july 7 1994 London, UK (1994-07-07)"
```

## Method 3: Reusable Function

```javascript
function removeAgePattern(str) {
    return str.replace(/\s*\(age \d+\)\s*/gi, ' ').trim();
}

// Test with different ages
console.log(removeAgePattern("july 7 1994 (age 7) London, UK (1994-07-07)"));
console.log(removeAgePattern("march 15 1990 (age 33) Paris, France"));
console.log(removeAgePattern("december 1 2000 (age 123) New York, USA"));
```

## Regex Explanation

| Pattern | Meaning |
|---------|---------|
| `\s*` | Matches zero or more whitespace characters |
| `\(` | Matches literal opening parenthesis |
| `age ` | Matches the text "age " |
| `\d+` | Matches one or more digits (any number) |
| `\)` | Matches literal closing parenthesis |
| `g` | Global flag - replaces all occurrences |
| `i` | Case-insensitive flag (optional) |

